1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:04,158
Welcome to Night 2 of the Cognitive Shutdown Method.

2
00:00:04,108 --> 00:00:11,564
Tonight is about the shutdown ritual, the transition between the wired world and the resting brain.

3
00:00:11,564 --> 00:00:14,373
The science is unambiguous.

4
00:00:14,373 --> 00:00:24,991
Screen light, especially in the blue-wavelength range, suppresses melatonin production by up to fifty percent for several hours after exposure.

5
00:00:24,991 --> 00:00:30,226
Melatonin is the chemical signal that tells your brain darkness is coming.

6
00:00:30,226 --> 00:00:34,211
Without it, your body does not know it is time to sleep.

7
00:00:34,211 --> 00:00:36,785
But the issue is deeper than light.

8
00:00:36,785 --> 00:00:48,741
Phones, tablets, laptops, and television keep your prefrontal cortex active, processing information, evaluating, comparing, scrolling.

9
00:00:48,741 --> 00:00:52,697
That is the opposite of what your brain needs to fall asleep.

10
00:00:52,697 --> 00:00:56,858
Sleep requires the prefrontal cortex to disengage.

11
00:00:56,858 --> 00:01:01,079
So tonight, you create a sixty-minute digital curfew.

12
00:01:01,079 --> 00:01:06,152
Sixty minutes before your intended bedtime, all screens go away.

13
00:01:06,152 --> 00:01:11,344
Phone in another room, on airplane mode, charging in the kitchen.

14
00:01:11,344 --> 00:01:13,270
Not on your nightstand.

15
00:01:13,270 --> 00:01:15,152
Not under your pillow.

16
00:01:15,152 --> 00:01:16,491
Out of reach.

17
00:01:16,491 --> 00:01:21,049
In that sixty-minute window, choose one quiet activity.

18
00:01:21,049 --> 00:01:22,932
Reading a physical book.

19
00:01:22,932 --> 00:01:24,594
Light stretching.

20
00:01:24,594 --> 00:01:26,417
A warm shower.

21
00:01:26,417 --> 00:01:27,638
Journaling.

22
00:01:27,638 --> 00:01:32,491
Anything that does not emit light and does not require active thinking.

23
00:01:32,491 --> 00:01:35,623
Now, let your body begin its descent.

24
00:01:35,623 --> 00:01:37,388
Soften your face.

25
00:01:37,388 --> 00:01:40,741
Let your hands rest open, palms up.

26
00:01:40,741 --> 00:01:44,623
Breathe in slowly through your nose for four seconds.

27
00:01:44,623 --> 00:01:47,285
Hold gently for seven seconds.

28
00:01:47,285 --> 00:01:50,299
Release through your mouth for eight seconds.

29
00:01:50,299 --> 00:01:51,476
Again.

30
00:01:51,476 --> 00:01:52,947
In for four.

31
00:01:52,947 --> 00:01:54,549
Hold for seven.

32
00:01:54,549 --> 00:01:55,917
Out for eight.

33
00:01:55,917 --> 00:01:57,476
One last time.

34
00:01:57,476 --> 00:01:58,947
In for four.

35
00:01:58,947 --> 00:02:00,549
Hold for seven.

36
00:02:00,549 --> 00:02:01,917
Out for eight.

37
00:02:01,917 --> 00:02:03,976
Your screens have stopped.

38
00:02:03,976 --> 00:02:06,873
Your brain knows now that night has begun.

39
00:02:06,873 --> 00:02:08,211
Sleep well.

